[F2] The intended tensor oracle is $G=\operatorname{WH}_{N^2}(u\otimes u)$;
for every tensor coordinate $q$, it satisfies
$G(q)=q\cdot(u\otimes u)$. ([[def-quadratic-equation-instance-and-tensor-code-oracles]])

[F1] In a supplied $G$-frame, curvature is $\Omega=d\omega+\omega\wedge\omega$;
its invariant-polynomial evaluation patches to a global form
([[def-evaluation-of-an-invariant-polynomial-on-curvature]]).

[F4] $\operatorname{WH}_n(u)$ is the truth table of $r\mapsto u\cdot r$;
when $n=0$ it is the one-entry zero table.
([[def-walsh-hadamard-encoding-and-relative-distance]])
